BEGIN_PGML
The values of several definite integrals are given as follows:

[```\int_0^3s(t)\,dt = 10 \quad \int_3^5s(t)\,dt = 8 \quad \int_3^5r(t)\,dt = -1 \quad \int_0^5r(t)\,dt = 11```]

Use these values and properties of definite integrals to evaluate the indicated definite integral.

Find a formula for [`a`] in terms of [`b`] such that [`\ds \int_0^5 \big(ar(t)+bs(t)\big) \, dt=0\text{.}`]

[_]{$a}{10}

END_PGML

